    {
      "id": "aether-sculpt",
      "title": "Aether Sculpt",
      "platform": "VR",
      "summary": "A hand-tracked volumetric sculpting tool for Meta Quest \u2014 no controllers, just gesture-based deformation of a live signed-distance mesh at 90fps.",
      "longDescription": "Aether Sculpt lets artists shape 3D forms with their bare hands in VR. It reads hand-tracking data from the Quest's cameras, maps finger positions to a deformation field, and updates a signed-distance-field mesh in real time using compute shaders.\n\nThe hardest part was keeping deformation feedback under one frame of latency so the sculpting felt physical rather than laggy \u2014 that meant moving most of the math off the CPU entirely.",
      "coverImage": "",
      "gallery": [],
      "videoUrl": "",
      "codeSnippet": "// Simplified SDF deformation kernel (HLSL compute shader)\nRWStructuredBuffer<float> field;\n\n[numthreads(8,8,8)]\nvoid CSMain(uint3 id : SV_DispatchThreadID) {\n    float3 p = IndexToWorld(id);\n    float d = field[Index(id)];\n    float brush = sdSphere(p - handPos, brushRadius);\n    field[Index(id)] = opSmoothUnion(d, brush, smoothing);\n}",
